questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot application experiences a gradual increase in Heap memory usage leading to an eventual `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` under sustained load. A code review reveals the following service component:

java
@Service
public class RequestProcessingService {
    private static final ThreadLocal<byte[]> REQUEST_BUFFER = new ThreadLocal<>();

    public void process(RequestData data) {
        byte[] buffer = REQUEST_BUFFER.get();
        if (buffer == null) {
            buffer = new byte[1024 * 1024]; // 1MB buffer allocation
            REQUEST_BUFFER.set(buffer);
        }
        // Perform processing logic
        helperMethod();
    }

    @Transactional
    public void helperMethod() {
        // Database persistence logic
    }
}


Heap dump analysis reveals that thousands of `byte[]` instances are strongly retained inside `ThreadLocalMap$Entry` objects belonging to `http-nio` worker threads.
